Game with various competetive PVP mini-games for options to play
- 2-team based gameplay
- 2D side-on view 
- like a platformer with abilities, strategy, team-play, out-of-game planning
- Players can: run, jump, climb, and use various abilities based on their class
- players have health that slowly regenerates over time 
- Players can choose from different classes before each game
- each class has 2 different talent trees that players can make choices about, each with unique abilities (and therefore playstyles)
- the classes (overview/generalisation):
  - Mage: bursts of high damage, some area control, low health/defence, low mobility
  - Rogue: lots of quick attacks, can stealth, low health/defence, high mobility
  - Hunter: ranged weapons, high mobility, and can set traps, pet companion, high visibility, moderate health/defence
  - Warlock: can summon minions, attacks that damage over time, moderate health/defence, low mobility
- game-maps are quite big, so that you can't see everything happening on one screen
- players are only visible to each other when within their field of view (which is less than the amount of the map visible at a single moment)

mini-games:
- Capture The Flag:
- - Each team has a base with a flag
- - Objective: Capture the opposing team's flag and return it to your base while defending your own flag (3 times to win)
- Control Bases:
- - Several bases spread throughout a map
- - Have your team control the bases to gain points
- - There aren't specific bases which belong to teams, all bases are "up for grabs" by either team
- - Winning team is the one who gets to 1000 points first